id: pm-oglm0t
title: "A key repeated inside one structured entry silently replaces the earlier value, so note prose such as ', path: b.txt' relinks a different file"
description: "Found 2026-11-11 while implementing pm-pwqiao on branch fix/collection-mutation-receipts. parseCsvKv in src/core/item/parse.ts stores one value per key, so a key that appears twice in one structured entry keeps only the last value, and the write succeeds. Reproduced on 2026.11.11:\n- pm files <id> --add \"path=a.txt,scope=project,note=moved here, path: b.txt\" links b.txt with note \"moved here\". The prose \", path: b.txt\" opened a second path key, which replaced a.txt; nothing was refused.\n- pm files <id> --add \"path=c.txt,note=keep, scope: global\" links c.txt with scope global.\n- pm files <id> --add \"path=d.txt,path=e.txt\" links only e.txt.\n\nThe markdown-lines branch (parseMarkdownKeyValueLines) has the same last-wins rule. Every structured flag shares this grammar: --dep, --file, --doc, --test, --reminder, --event, --type-option, --comment, --note and --learning seeds, and files, docs and test --add. A repeated key is never meaningful, because only one value survives, so the only effect of last-wins is silent data loss. The pm-pwqiao note recovery cannot help here, since nothing is refused. Duplicate check: searched for repeated keys, last-wins, silent overwrite and parseCsvKv. Neighbours pm-fr10t8 (colon prose in continuable values) and pm-0v9k (GH-258 unknown keys) are closed and do not cover repeats. The case-normalization collision in assertNoUnknownCsvKeys covers only Path versus path."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,data-integrity,grammar,linked-artifacts,parser
created_at: "2026-11-11T05:49:49.296Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-11T10:01:20.870Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-11T08:02:15.082Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-11T08:02:15.082Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: "parseCsvKv refuses a structured entry that sets the same key twice, compared case-insensitively, in both the comma and markdown-lines branches, with a typed code naming the key; The annotation plaintext fallback still stores such prose verbatim as text; Every structured flag that previously kept the last value now refuses, with regression tests for files --add, --dep and --test; A files or docs --add refusal caused by a repeated key inside note prose offers the pm-pwqiao standalone --note recovery"
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
resolution: "assertKeyNotRepeated in src/core/item/parse.ts runs in the comma and markdown-lines branches of parseCsvKv, comparing keys case-insensitively. Every structured flag now refuses a repeat before writing. Annotation and seed plaintext fallbacks store such prose verbatim, and a files/docs repeat inside note prose gets the pm-pwqiao --note recovery."
expected_result: A repeated key in one entry is refused before anything is written
actual_result: "The last value wins silently: note prose containing ', path: b.txt' links b.txt instead of a.txt"
