notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-11T06:43:26.102Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation on branch fix/collection-mutation-receipts (2026-11-11). assertKeyNotRepeated in src/core/item/parse.ts runs in both the comma branch of parseCsvKv and parseMarkdownKeyValueLines. A key that one entry already set, compared case-insensitively, is refused with code structured_entry_key_repeated, flag, value and details {repeated_key, first_key}. Continuation prose is unaffected, because only an identifier-shaped segment with a delimiter reaches the check.\n\nCallers that fall back to plaintext keep working: the --comment, --note and --learning seeds and the annotation --add path catch the refusal. Before this change, 'text=a, text=b' stored only 'b' and lost 'a, '. It now stores the raw entry verbatim, which loses nothing. The leftover 'text=' prefix in that fallback is pm-fr10t8's territory.\n\nRegression specs: parse-utils.spec.ts covers both grammars and Path/path; linked-artifact-note-recovery.spec.ts covers files --add, --dep and test --add."
